Z||000000||Back On Holiday||10-03-2001||06:06 PM||||Today, after replacing the fuel pump(at the advice of the Forum!) I dropped her down on the ground, and with the wife crossing her fingers, cranked her over for the first time.  she sputtered for a few seconds and then stalled, I started her up again and she purred.<BR>Of course, I have to replace a front brake line that is leaking, or I could have taken her down the road a few hundred feet...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I can't believe how smooth the clutch linkage and the throttle linkage is compared to the 84se I have.<BR>I will try and post some pics in the next week or so.<BR>I put her outside the garage for the first time in awhile, her red door that I got at the junkyard is still on the silver car (long story but I needed the silver door for the 84se - I replaced the skin on the 84 and the other door is awaiting its re-installment on the rest of the car)Red door...dunno what I'll do with it once I take it off, its a maroon color.<BR>had to put decklid on, it looks naked without a wing like the 84 has (an 86 decklid on an 84se)<BR>now, I gotta put the 84 in the garage to find out what wire is shorting on the engine.<BR><P>------------------<BR>84se Silver 2m4<BR>86se Silver 2m6||||reg||4
Z||000001||8Ball||10-03-2001||10:02 PM||||Sweet! I am hopeing to have my 86 v6 2m6 on the road within a week||||reg||1
